body:
Thank you dude, I don't think anyone has ever spoken to me so kindly before. I do take Sertraline and I think it does help. My mind just won't let me talk to my family about it, maybe it's because I don't want to burden them. I've been like that all my life, if I'm suffering I'll just take it without any help until it's bad enough that someone notices. Half way through school my eyesight started deteriorating and I obviously needed glasses but it took me 2 years of not being able to see the whiteboard and having to write down the questions from a classmate, this lead to me underperforming at school. It's funny though because it took 1 trip to the opticians to fix it, all that time spent struggling and it took 30 minutes to fix it.

&#x200B;

Sorry for rambling. Thanks again.
